vim is the Vim/Neovim editor. This sheet reflects the current Neovim config
(`~/.config/nvim`) plus the most useful built-in motions. Leader = `,`.

Current configuration:
	Leader / LocalLeader - `,`
	Normal ,tn - Edit a new tab (`:tabedit`)
	Normal ,tc - Close the current tab
	Normal ,cd - Change directory to the current file
	Normal ,xo or Space - Cycle to the next window
	Normal ,wh / ,wj / ,wk / ,wl - Focus left/down/up/right window
	Normal sh / sj / sk / sl - Focus left/down/up/right window
	Normal ,x1 - Keep only the current window
	Normal ,x2 or ss - Horizontal split
	Normal ,x3 or sv - Vertical split
	Normal Ctrl+Arrow - Resize the current window by 2
	Normal Shift+j/k - Next/previous buffer
	Normal ,xs - Save the current file
	Normal ,xm - Open the command-line prompt
	Normal x - Delete without yanking
	Normal Ctrl+d - Delete the previous word without yanking
	Normal +/- - Increment/decrement number
	Insert kj - Return to Normal mode
	Visual < / > - Indent and keep the selection
	Visual Alt+j/k - Move selected lines down/up
	Visual p - Paste without replacing the yank register
	Normal/Visual ,rb - Start substitute; Normal uses the whole file
	Terminal Ctrl+h/j/k/l - Leave terminal mode and move by direction

Plugin and language mappings:
	Normal ,e - Toggle NvimTree
	Normal ,rr - Find files (Telescope)
	Normal ,dd - Live grep (Telescope)
	Normal ,bb - List buffers (Telescope)
	Normal ;t - Help tags; ;; - Resume the last picker
	Normal ;e - Diagnostics; ,kk - Show keymaps
	Normal ,xf - File browser for the current directory
	Normal ,ff - Toggle ZenMode
	Normal ,ll / ,l{motion} - Comment toggle (Comment.nvim)
	Normal/Visual ys{motion}{char} - Add surround
	Normal ds{char} - Delete surround; cs{old}{new} - Change surround
	Insert Alt+e - Autopairs fast-wrap
	Insert Ctrl+p/n - Previous/next completion item
	Insert Ctrl+Space - Trigger completion; Ctrl+e - Cancel it
	Insert Enter - Confirm the selected completion
	Insert Tab / Shift+Tab - Completion and snippet navigation
	LSP Normal gd/gD/gi/gr - Definition/declaration/implementation/references
	LSP Normal K - Hover; ,rn - Rename; ,ca - Code action
	LSP Normal ,lf - Format; [d / ]d - Previous/next diagnostic
	LSP Normal ,df - Show the current-line diagnostic

Built-in Normal mode:
	h/j/k/l - Move left/down/up/right
	w/b/e - Move by word; 0/$ - Start/end of line
	gg/G - Start/end of buffer
	i/a/o/O - Insert before/after, or open a line below/above
	v/V/Ctrl+v - Character/line/blockwise Visual mode
	y/d/c - Yank/delete/change; p/P - Paste after/before
	u / Ctrl+r - Undo/redo; . - Repeat the last change
	/ or ? - Search forward/backward; n/N - Next/previous match
	: - Enter Ex command-line; Ctrl+w then h/j/k/l - Move windows

See `~/.config/nvim/docs/guide/keymaps.md` for the complete plugin and mode matrix.
